WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.930
- Over the years, I've had
some issues regarding anxiety

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:06.950
and depression and one of
the things that I thought

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:10.720
might help me would be to get a pug.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.810
I adopted a pug puppy.

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:15.720
His name is Phil, and I've had Phil

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.060
since he was eight weeks old

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:18.530
and could fit in the palm of my hand.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:21.040
Before I got Phil, when I was feeling bad,

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.060
I would look at pictures of pugs,

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.930
because they're so cute
that they look like

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:25.960
they shouldn't exist.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.900
They look like a gift from
an ancient civilization

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:29.930
that we've unearthed and we're like,

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:32.270
"I can't believe that they made this!"

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:34.530
Phil can accurately be described

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:36.040
as the runt of the litter,

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.610
but what he lacks in size,

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:41.060
he has magnified many
times over in cuteness.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:44.140
His favorite things are hanging
out on the couch with me,

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:45.290
going on a walk with me,

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:46.620
kissing my face,

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.590
and chasing a laser beam,
we do that late every night.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:50.690
I'm a novelist.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:53.270
I've been having a little
trouble selling a book.

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:56.880
Finally though, I got a break
and this publisher asked me

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.170
to write a book for them,

00:00:58.170 --> 00:00:59.980
and I was over the moon

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:02.530
because this was guaranteed income,

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:05.460
so I just toiled on this
thing for months and months,

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.180
kind of going through savings,

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:09.610
and then after about nine
months of really hard work,

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:11.460
I got a call from my agent.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.130
She called and told me

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:15.780
that the book contract was being canceled

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.430
for reasons out of our control.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:19.570
I felt like I just need one break,

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:21.130
and I thought that book was the break,

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:23.690
and then it broke.

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:25.380
So I hung up with my agent,

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:28.760
I definitely very quickly
wound up on the floor,

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:30.620
and I laid there for a while,

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.170
just kind of spiraling down,

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:34.720
and Phil wandered into the room.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:37.630
Now the thing about Phil
is that if I'm laying down,

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:38.620
if I'm bending over,

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:41.720
if my face is in any gravitational way

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:45.110
accessible to him, he will
kiss it over and over and over,

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:47.920
but instead of doing that,
he saw me laying there

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:49.540
and he did the same,
that he had never done,

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:51.510
where he just kind of tilted
his head back and forth

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.260
like he didn't understand
what he was seeing,

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:56.130
then he kind of trotted over
to the other side of the room,

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:57.760
got his favorite rope toy,

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.950
and I thought he was gonna
bring it over to me to play

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:00.783
and I was like,

00:02:00.783 --> 00:02:01.616
"I'm not gonna be able to play."

00:02:01.616 --> 00:02:02.550
But he didn't do that,

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:07.040
he just kind of buried his
face in my side, near my heart,

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:09.080
which felt like it was breaking.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:12.090
In that moment, he did
literally the one thing on earth

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:15.840
that could unbreak it,
which was just to love me.

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:20.090
He loves me and doesn't
want me to be hurting,

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:22.120
and that's exactly how I feel about him.

00:02:23.477 --> 00:02:26.060
(upbeat music)

